  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 157 AM MDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nNorthwest flow aloft continues today as an area of low pressure in \nCanada continues to move northeastward and high pressure is allowed \nto build in along the West Coast. Wildfire smoke continues to\nfilter into Eastern Idaho, though some improvements are expected\nover the next few days. This ridge will amplify on \nThursday and be directly \"overhead\" on Friday. High pressure \nremains in control through the weekend. Next Monday, a low \nbegins to move into the western coast of British Columbia to \nflatten the ridge and move it eastward just a bit. All of this \nto say, get ready for the heat to return. Highs will be about 5 \ndegrees warmer today than yesterday, meaning we will make it \nback into the upper 80s to low 90s throughout the Snake River \nPlain. As we continue to heat up, expect highs to approach \ntriple digits in the eastern Magic Valley as early as Thursday \nafternoon with the rest of the Snake River Plain following suit \non Friday and Saturday. On Friday, the NBM shows a 40 to 50 \npercent chance of reaching 100 degrees from Burley to Pocatello.\nThat chance is higher out across the Arco Desert area. Chances \nare very similar on Saturday. By early next week, highs will be \na few degrees cooler thanks to the flattening of the ridge, but \nstill in the low to mid 90s for many. This slight pattern chance\nshould bring back some monsoon moisture next week, but \nspecifics of that are still several days away from coming into \nbetter focus.",
